  "slug": "intestinal-liver-mice-0dd6",
  "summary": "NAR database updates and cohort atlases arrive together, mapping GWAS, methylation, spatial and kinase data onto finer cellular and molecular contexts.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is consolidation of heterogeneous molecular evidence into annotated, queryable resources that embed analysis modules rather than serving raw data. scGWAS-DB maps 3,649 GWAS datasets onto single-cell atlases spanning 74 tissues and 1,713 cell types. MethMarkerDB 2.0 extends methylation biomarkers to 21 cancer types and adds CpG-level and functional modules. CROST 2.0 reaches 544 spatial transcriptomics projects (3,538 samples) and adds niche, colocalization and cancer-niche tools. KinaseMD 2.0, Gene Expression Nebulas 2.0 and iCellOmics (17 industrially relevant cell lines) update mutation–drug response, curated transcriptomic and multi-omic–phenotype content. Atlas-scale efforts follow the same pattern. PANGEA remaps 12.6M cells into a 165-subtype hierarchy across 160 diseases. CCGA harmonizes 667 canine tumor-normal exomes and reports 39 drivers. A 1,824-tumor lung RNA-seq cohort defines nine transcriptional clusters with an interactive portal. Kinetic-model, natural-product network and CellChat Hotspot work contributes reusable analytical frameworks rather than resources.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-16"
}
